course: dictionary
lesson: 5070
title: Instead: one thing in place of another
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: «Instead» means in place of something else. «We had no milk, so we drank water instead.» The water takes the place of the milk. When you see instead, look for the thing that has been left out.
explain: «Instead of» comes before the thing that is replaced. In «tea instead of coffee», you have tea, and coffee is the one you did not choose. In «say Thank you instead of disagreeing», the thank you takes the place of the disagreeing.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Some rare birds lay a second egg if the first is taken, so a zoo can hatch two chicks instead of one.» Swap in your meaning: the zoo hatches two chicks in place of one. It makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: Instead means in place of something else.
fact: «Instead of» comes before the thing that is replaced: «tea instead of coffee».
fact: «Singapore Zoo uses moats and plants instead of bars.» The bars are the thing that is not used.
fact: In a maths problem, if the first number changes, the answer changes too, so you must work the problem out again.
fact: In a story, a plan can change: someone does one thing instead of what they first meant to do.
exercise: «We had no milk, so we drank water instead.» What does instead mean here? | In the middle of the milk | Very quickly | Before the milk | *In place of the milk
exercise: «Say Thank you instead of disagreeing.» Which thing is replaced? | Thank you | A bow | A smile | *Disagreeing
exercise: «Singapore Zoo uses moats and plants instead of bars.» What is used instead of bars? | The Night Safari | *Moats and plants | Lions | Bars
test: Tom had no pen, so he used a pencil instead. What does instead tell you? | He lost his pencil | He used a pen twice | He wrote nothing at all | *He used a pencil in place of a pen
test: «Real toads walk slowly to their ponds instead of driving cars into them.» What do real toads NOT do? | Walk slowly | Move on land | *Drive cars | Go to their ponds
exam: If at the start I had put two pears instead, what must you do with the rest of a maths problem? | *Work it out again with the new number | Keep the old answer | Write the answer in pears only | Skip the problem
